{"name":"Winged Victory","hex":"#ebe4e2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winged","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having wings.","Having wings of a specified kind."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of wing"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winged"},{"term":"victory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The condition or state of having won a battle or competition, or having succeeded in an effort;  an instance of this.","Alternative letter-case form of Victory (“ the Roman goddess of victory, the counterpart of the Greek goddess Nike; also , an artistic depiction of her, chiefly as a winged woman”)."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used to encourage someone to achieve success, or to celebrate a success or triumph."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/victory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winged Victory (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Winged Victory is a 1944 American war drama film directed by George Cukor, a joint effort of 20th Century-Fox and the U.S. Army Air Forces. Based upon the 1943 play of the same name by Moss Hart, who also wrote the screenplay, the film opened only after the play's theatre run. The film version of Winged Victory used many of the Broadway cast, who were brought to Hollywood."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Winged_Victory%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winged_Victory_(film)"},{"title":"Winged Victory (Lewis)","blocks":[{"text":"Winged Victory is a World War I memorial in the U.S. state of Washington, which consists of four figures of uniformed persons atop a granite pedestal eclipsed by a fifth figure depicting the Winged Victory of Samothrace."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_close_view_06.jpg/330px-Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_close_view_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winged_Victory_(Lewis)"},{"title":"Winged Victory of Samothrace","blocks":[{"text":"The Winged Victory of Samothrace, or the Nike of Samothrace, is a votive monument originally discovered on the island of Samothrace in the northeastern Aegean Sea. It is a masterpiece of Greek sculpture from the Hellenistic era, dating from the beginning of the 2nd century BC. It is composed of a statue representing the goddess Nike (Victory), whose head and arms are missing, and a base in the shape of a ship's bow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Victoire_de_Samothrace_-_Musee_du_Louvre_-_20190812.jpg/330px-Victoire_de_Samothrace_-_Musee_du_Louvre_-_20190812.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winged_Victory_of_Samothrace"},{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Winged_Victory1.jpg/500px-Winged_Victory1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Winged_Victory1.jpg/1280px-Winged_Victory1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Winged_Victory1.jpg/500px-Winged_Victory1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Winged Victory pictured in 1938","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWinged_Victory1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_detail_02.jpg/500px-Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_detail_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_detail_02.jpg/1280px-Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_detail_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_detail_02.jpg/500px-Washington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_detail_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail view, 2020","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWashington_State_Capitol_-_Winged_Victory_-_detail_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/WACapitolInsuranceBldg.jpg/500px-WACapitolInsuranceBldg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/WACapitolInsuranceBldg.jpg/1280px-WACapitolInsuranceBldg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/WACapitolInsuranceBldg.jpg/500px-WACapitolInsuranceBldg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A side view of Winged Victory pictured in 2006, a period during which the statue was painted in a golden hue.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWACapitolInsuranceBldg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or